From a33ec2b27e85f6b28260619b07c222eb44ef6cae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:51:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/47] Z 6III MCU: SPI and TIM1/8 compare interrupts, switch
 snapshot, live view starts

With these the body MCU's own firmware takes the camera as far as the
synthetic peer with mcu-camctl-reply=on did: the MCU sends its key
report, answers the EXPEED's family-9 mode command (kind 2 -> kind 3)
itself, the display comes on, and CAPST enters mode 1 (capture trace
category 0x1a, code 0x7835) -- live view starts.

- SPI1-6 drive their interrupt line, level-sensitive: TXE with TXEIE or
  RXNE with RXNEIE while SPE is set (both flags always read set). The
  SbCtl task's HAL interrupt-driven sends on SPI3 waited for a TXE
  interrupt that never came; now its family-10 requests get answered.
  (SbCtl/SbMng look like the Speedlight -- hot-shoe -- service: status
  1 is "nothing on the shoe", which the EXPEED keeps polling.)
- TIM1 and TIM8 compare matches go to their own vectors (27, 46) through
  a second sysbus IRQ on stm32f2xx_timer, IRQ 0 when it is not wired.
  SbCtl's transfer timeout is a TIM1 channel 2 match.
- TIMx_CNT reads wrap at ARR, as the counter does.
- "ccr-wraps", a declared deviation on stm32f2xx_timer, off by default
  and on for this MCU: a CCRx beyond ARR matches at CCRx mod (ARR + 1).
  The switch service arms TIM10 (ARR 499) at CCR1 = CNT + 500 for its
  first snapshot of the switches; only that match's callback takes the
  snapshot, and only the snapshot lets SwMng send the key report, which
  is what the EXPEED waits for before it sends the mode command. RM0386
  says such a match never happens, yet the camera does get its key
  report; until that is explained this reads the firmware's "one period
  later" as it plainly means it. Each channel that uses it is named on
  stderr.
- SPI enables are named four times per SPI, not every time (SPI4 is
  re-enabled for every frame).
- gdb_probe.py ATTACH=1 attaches to a running machine's stub (the A53s,
  process 1) instead of starting one.

Next on the path: the EXPEED has not raised its capture-sync request
(GPIO port 3 bit 12) yet, and that pair of wires is not connected to
the MCU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
